  "description": "A copy of the r-fmt-2b-w-accdb fixture (123 pages; page 122, Au4's old data page, is the only free page inside the file). Au1: tdef 107, usage maps 108, PK root 109, ten rows (IDs 1-10, 21-23 bytes) on data page 110. One shared session opens a table-type recordset on Au1 (RecordCount read) and runs Delete then MoveNext three times; after each, the recordset's RecordCount and TableDefs(\"Au1\").RecordCount are read, and after a 1.5 s pause the pages. A second table-type recordset is then opened (RecordCount read, closed). The first closes (pause, counts, pages), then the database (pages). Asks whether a table-type Delete writes the TableDef's row count with the row or at the recordset's Close, as a dynaset's does (r-q17 retire-rs-delete-au1). Each read keeps page 0 bytes 3584-3591 and pages 1, 107, 108, 109, 110, 122; after Close every page's hash too.",
